00:33:58.895 --> 00:34:00.175
And I said, well,

00:34:00.415 --> 00:34:02.255
that was the reason that

00:34:02.575 --> 00:34:07.620
the applicant came in to subdivide the property first and the site plan second

00:34:08.180 --> 00:34:08.980
is

00:34:08.980 --> 00:34:15.460
so that they, you know, one of the reasons could have been, you know, they just wanted to deal with dividing the property first.

00:34:16.260 --> 00:34:21.300
It could have been that they didn't want to, you know, deal with all the subdivision regulations.

00:34:21.755 --> 00:34:22.635
I don't know.

00:34:23.835 --> 00:34:27.355
But again, having done our due diligence, we had the fire marshal

00:34:28.555 --> 00:34:30.475
and the town engineer at the time

00:34:30.795 --> 00:34:32.875
take a look at the application,

00:34:32.955 --> 00:34:35.115
and they both thought it was satisfactory,

00:34:35.750 --> 00:34:37.350
And in fact, it supports

00:34:37.510 --> 00:34:38.630
the Connecticut

00:34:38.630 --> 00:34:39.750
Safety Code.

00:34:42.470 --> 00:34:48.550
But I went back and talked to Mark Grants about that. He pointed me out to this section

00:34:49.155 --> 00:34:57.155
in our regulations and I wanted to share that with everybody because it was kind of eye opening to me tonight. I probably should have

00:34:57.555 --> 00:34:58.675
color coded it here.

00:35:04.050 --> 00:35:05.330
So when we're

00:35:05.970 --> 00:35:08.210
looking at compliance with regulations,

00:35:08.210 --> 00:35:11.410
you know, it says it's going to conform in all respects with these regulations,

00:35:11.410 --> 00:35:12.450
less variance,

00:35:12.610 --> 00:35:13.250
blah, blah, blah.

00:35:14.615 --> 00:35:15.335
Further,

00:35:15.415 --> 00:35:17.495
the application shall conform

00:35:17.495 --> 00:35:20.775
to the Andover subdivision regulations.

00:35:21.815 --> 00:35:26.695
So even though the applicant in this case came in with a site plan,

00:35:28.290 --> 00:35:29.490
we can still

00:35:29.890 --> 00:35:30.770
require

00:35:31.010 --> 00:35:33.170
and should require compliance

00:35:33.570 --> 00:35:36.130
with the Andover subdivision regulations,

00:35:36.850 --> 00:35:39.890
which state that a commercial building will have a sprinkler system in it.

00:35:41.265 --> 00:35:46.465
You would think that the applicant would have wanted to put a sprinkler system in there for his own protection.

00:35:49.745 --> 00:35:54.385
But I figured that was his problem. But, you know, the lesson learned for me

00:35:54.800 --> 00:35:57.920
is we're allowed to enforce our

00:35:57.920 --> 00:35:58.720
subdivision

00:35:58.720 --> 00:35:59.920
regulations,

00:36:01.040 --> 00:36:04.240
even though we're only doing a site plan review.

00:36:05.120 --> 00:36:07.760
And so I wanted to share that with all you guys.

00:36:10.425 --> 00:36:14.905
And I think that gives us a little bit of latitude on

00:36:14.905 --> 00:36:15.465
how

00:36:16.505 --> 00:36:18.345
to get a better product going forward.

00:36:18.665 --> 00:36:19.625
